                <pb facs="0998" n="878" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg878"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Johnson Electoral Mission/204:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hanna</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-03T14:00:00-04:00">June 3, 1931—2
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>129. Legation’s 91, May 29, 3 p.m. Please report by telegraph whether the
                    National Board of Elections of Nicaragua normally functions in connection with
                    municipal elections and has jurisdiction over same. If so, explain fully to what
                    extent and cite appropriate laws.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
